Subject: [PATCH 113/121] spec: FlashInfer radix top-k for the sparse verify
 (SGLANG_OPT_SPEC_SPARSE_TOPK)

torch.topk over the fp32 verify logits (V = 248320) is the largest piece of
the sparse verify. FlashInfer's top_k with sorted=True, deterministic=True
sorts on device (no torch.sort + gather) and matches torch.topk values bit for
bit on randn/peaked/ties/masked rows (k 64/128, 1-32 rows). CUDA-graph GPU time
per call on RTX PRO 6000 (k=64): 63.6 -> 28.0 us at 4 rows, 60.9 -> 28.9 us at
8, 68.6 -> 30.4 us at 16.

Off by default. The topk module is JIT-built on first use, so enable it only
with a FlashInfer cache that already holds a built topk module.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
